-- =============================================================================
-- University of Nigeria, Nsukka — Faculty of Social Sciences — Political Science
-- Course outlines transcribed from the Faculty of Social Sciences course
-- handbook (scanned copy), covering the Four-Year Standard Undergraduate
-- Programme in Political Science: all four years, both semesters, including
-- required ancillary, general-studies and elective courses.
-- =============================================================================
-- Run in the Supabase SQL Editor. Safe to run more than once: existing rows
-- for this department are removed first, so it updates rather than duplicates.
--
-- SEMESTERS: for 100, 200 and 400 Level, the handbook explicitly labels every
-- course "FIRST SEMESTER" or "SECOND SEMESTER" in its programme-structure
-- tables, so those stated values are used directly.
--
-- THIRD YEAR: the 300 Level programme-structure table itself was not present
-- in this scan (the pages jump from the Second Year table straight to the
-- Fourth Year table — the same kind of page gap seen elsewhere in this
-- document). The 300-level courses below are real — each has its own
-- printed code/title/unit-count on a "COURSE DESCRIPTION" page — but with no
-- structure table to read their semester from, semester is assigned using
-- this app's documented fallback (an odd final digit means first semester,
-- an even one means second), the same convention already used and disclosed
-- for UNN Geology's outline. Correct any that differ at UNN via the Table
-- Editor.
--
-- One page of course descriptions (around PDF page 68 of the scan) was
-- photographed too blurred to transcribe; whatever course(s) it held are
-- left out rather than guessed at.
--
-- ANCILLARY/GSP/ELECTIVE COURSES FROM OTHER DEPARTMENTS: courses such as
-- COS 101/304, GEO 131, GSP 1xx/2xx, PSY 101 and FSS 201/202 appear in the
-- Political Science timetable but their own descriptions are not printed in
-- the Political Science section of this document, so they carry real
-- code/title/units only, description left blank.
-- =============================================================================

delete from public.course_outlines
 where institution = 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka'
   and department = 'Political Science';

insert into public.course_outlines
  (course_code, course_title, institution, faculty, department, level,
   semester, credit_units, description, topics, contributor_name)
values
  ('PSC 101', 'Introduction to Political Science I', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '100 Level', 'first', 2, 'The course introduces students to the nature of politics and how it is played; it emphasizes the issues of political discourse and practice; it also introduces students to the language and basic concepts of political science and other disciplines.', '["The course introduces students to the nature of politics and how it is played", "It emphasizes the issues of political discourse and practice", "It also introduces students to the language and basic concepts of political science and other disciplines"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 111', 'Nigerian Constitutional Development', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '100 Level', 'first', 2, 'The course introduces students to the different phases in Nigerian constitutional development in a chronological and sequential order; emphasis is on Colonialism, the Richards Constitution, the Macpherson Constitution, the Lyttleton Constitution, the Independence Constitution, the Republican Constitution and the 1999 Constitution.', '["The course introduces students to the different phases in Nigerian constitutional development in a chronological and sequential order", "Emphasis is on Colonialism, the Richards Constitution, the Macpherson Constitution, the Lyttleton Constitution", "The Independence Constitution, the Republican Constitution and the 1999 Constitution"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 113', 'Nigerian Legal System', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '100 Level', 'first', 2, 'The course introduces students to the Nigerian Legal System; emphasis is placed on the social, economic and political environment within which the Nigerian legal system emerged and in which it functions; the impact of the Nigerian legal system on Nigerian government and politics, and the use and abuse of law as an instrument of government and politics.', '["The course introduces students to the Nigerian Legal System", "Emphasis is placed on the social, economic and political environment within which the Nigerian legal system emerged and in which it functions", "The impact of the Nigerian legal system on Nigerian government and politics", "The use and abuse of law as an instrument of government and politics"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 131', 'Introduction to Public Administration', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '100 Level', 'first', 2, 'The course introduces students to the basic concepts of Public Administration; public and private administration; Public Administration as an Art and as a Science; Public Administration and other social sciences; dimensions of Public Administration; general aspects of administration; approaches to the study of Public Administration; and environment of Public Administration.', '["The course introduces students to the basic concepts of Public Administration; public and private administration", "Public Administration as an Art and as a Science", "Public Administration and other social sciences; dimensions of Public Administration", "General aspects of administration; approaches to the study of Public Administration", "Environment of Public Administration"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 102', 'Introduction to Political Science II', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '100 Level', 'second', 2, 'The course introduces students to the methods of Political Science, as well as the theory of knowledge; the relationship between political science and other disciplines.', '["The course introduces students to the methods of Political Science, as well as the theory of knowledge", "The relationship between political science and other disciplines"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 112', 'Introduction to African Politics', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '100 Level', 'second', 2, 'The course introduces students to the Nature of African politics; origins and problems of African politics; Problems of colonialism, neo-colonialism, succession to power, military rule; Africa and the colonial metropolis, and Africa in international affairs.', '["The course introduces students to the Nature of African politics; origins and problems of African politics", "Problems of colonialism, neo-colonialism, succession to power, military rule", "Africa and the colonial metropolis, and Africa in international affairs"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 114', 'Introduction to Strategic Studies', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '100 Level', 'second', 2, 'The course introduces students to the basic concepts in war and strategic thinking; differences between tactics, grand tactics, strategy, grand strategy, theatre strategy; deterrence; sphere of influence, sphere of interest, pre-emptive strike, alliance; the basics of military organization; strategic resources, geopolitics, the State as Rational Actor; regional security threat; intelligence and information warfare; alliance (military); asymmetrical warfare (insurgency and terrorism); nuclear weapons and weapons of mass destruction (WMD); defense spending; theories of strategy and war; Schools of military strategy: Clausewitz, Sun Tzu, and John Boyd.', '["The course introduces students to the basic concepts in war and strategic thinking", "Differences between tactics, grand tactics, strategy, grand strategy, theatre strategy; deterrence", "Sphere of influence, sphere of interest, pre-emptive strike, alliance; the basics of military organization", "Strategic resources, geopolitics, the State as Rational Actor; regional security threat", "Intelligence and information warfare; alliance (military); asymmetrical warfare (insurgency and terrorism)", "Nuclear weapons and weapons of mass destruction (WMD); defense spending", "Theories of strategy and war; Schools of military strategy: Clausewitz, Sun Tzu, and John Boyd"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 116', 'Organization of Government, the Citizen and the State', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '100 Level', 'second', 2, 'The course introduces students to the various ways of organizing governments; theory of separation of powers; forms of political and administrative systems: Unitarian, Federalism, Confederalism; forms of government; instrumentalities of political interaction like political parties, pressure groups, interest groups; relationship of the citizen to the state; duties and obligations of the citizen to the state; nature of strained relations and the processes of rectification; political obligation, basis of freedom, loyalty and patriotism.', '["The course introduces students to the various ways of organizing governments; theory of separation of powers", "Forms of political and administrative systems: Unitarian, Federalism, Confederalism", "Forms of government; instrumentalities of political interaction like political parties, pressure groups, interest groups", "Relationship of the citizen to the state; duties and obligations of the citizen to the state", "Nature of strained relations and the processes of rectification", "Political obligation, basis of freedom, loyalty and patriotism"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 118', 'Introduction to Comparative Politics', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '100 Level', 'second', 2, 'The course introduces students to the meaning and nature of comparative politics; logic of comparative social inquiry; objectives of comparative inquiry; approaches to the study of comparative politics – single-country approach, multi-country approach, synchronic approach, and problems of comparative politics.', '["The course introduces students to the meaning and nature of comparative politics; logic of comparative social inquiry", "Objectives of comparative inquiry", "Approaches to the study of comparative politics – single-country approach, multi-country approach, synchronic approach", "Problems of comparative politics"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 122', 'Introduction to International Politics', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '100 Level', 'second', 2, 'The course introduces students to the organization of the international society; theories of international politics; linkage politics; theory of coalition and alliances; Balance of power theory, and impact of the emergence of the developing world.', '["The course introduces students to the organization of the international society; theories of international politics", "Linkage politics; theory of coalition and alliances", "Balance of power theory, and impact of the emergence of the developing world"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 182', 'Industrial Training/Field Trip', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '100 Level', 'second', 2, 'The course involves study tours and attachment to selected international institutions, ministries, diplomatic missions and other agencies relevant to the study and practical aspects of politics, public and private administration; with written reports at the conclusion of the study tours and attachment. The students can go to Alliance Française, Goethe Institute or any other language-learning institute for language courses. They can also go for computer proficiency courses.', '["The course involves study tours and attachment to selected international institutions, ministries, diplomatic missions and other agencies relevant to the study and practical aspects of politics, public and private administration", "Written reports at the conclusion of the study tours and attachment", "The students can go to Alliance Française, Goethe Institute or any other language-learning institute for language courses, or for computer proficiency courses"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 201', 'Introduction to Political Analysis', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '200 Level', 'first', 2, 'The course introduces students to the nature of political systems and the structure of government, political representation and institutions of different regimes; the relationship between regime types and political efficiency; citizen participation and political culture; theoretical and conceptual approaches to political analysis.', '["The course introduces students to the nature of political systems and the structure of government, political representation and institutions of different regimes", "The relationship between regime types and political efficiency", "Citizen participation and political culture", "Theoretical and conceptual approaches to political analysis"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 211', 'Nigerian Government and Politics', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '200 Level', 'first', 2, 'The course introduces students to the general politics, economic and social frameworks within which Nigerian politics and the governmental institutions develop and function, treated within a historical perspective; the federal arrangements and division of powers; critical issues in Nigerian politics: Census, elections, education, ethnic relations, representation and representativeness.', '["The course introduces students to the general politics, economic and social frameworks within which Nigerian politics and the governmental institutions develop and function, treated within a historical perspective", "The federal arrangements and division of powers", "Critical issues in Nigerian politics: Census, elections, education, ethnic relations, representation and representativeness"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 213', 'Methodology of Comparative Politics', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '200 Level', 'first', 2, 'The course introduces students to comparative political analysis; history of comparative politics; the scientific method, logic of comparison; classification systems; competing paradigms or orientations in comparative political analysis; cross-system theorizing; and measurement problems in cross-national research.', '["The course introduces students to comparative political analysis; history of comparative politics", "The scientific method, logic of comparison; classification systems", "Competing paradigms or orientations in comparative political analysis", "Cross-system theorizing; and measurement problems in cross-national research"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 221', 'Foreign Policy Analysis', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '200 Level', 'first', 2, 'The course introduces students to the analysis of patterns, approaches and styles of decision-making and formulation of strategies in the formulation, packaging, implementation of foreign policies of states in international relations; provides a descriptive and explanatory framework to predict, review and evaluate the foreign policy of states and other foreign policy analysis; Determinants of foreign policy; principles, objectives of foreign policy; approaches to the study of foreign policy analysis; problems of foreign policy analysis.', '["The course introduces students to the analysis of patterns, approaches and styles of decision-making and formulation of strategies in the formulation, packaging, implementation of foreign policies of states in international relations", "Provides a descriptive and explanatory framework to predict, review and evaluate the foreign policy of states and other foreign policy analysis", "Determinants of foreign policy; principles, objectives of foreign policy", "Approaches to the study of foreign policy analysis; problems of foreign policy analysis"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 223', 'American Politics and Constitutional Democracy', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '200 Level', 'first', 2, 'The course introduces students to the core values and beliefs of the United States of America: equality, life, justice, liberty, common good, diversity, popular sovereignty, patriotism; fundamental principles of America - rule of law, checks and balances, representative government, separation of powers, freedom of religion, individual rights, federalism, and civil society.', '["The course introduces students to the core values and beliefs of the United States of America: equality, life, justice, liberty, common good, diversity, popular sovereignty, patriotism", "Fundamental principles of America - rule of law, checks and balances, representative government, separation of powers, freedom of religion, individual rights, federalism, and civil society"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 231', 'Principles of Public Administration', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '200 Level', 'first', 2, 'The course introduces students to the rationale of administration; the ecology of administration; the politics of administration, the administrative actor, delegation, administrative audit and control element of Administrative Law.', '["The course introduces students to the rationale of administration; the ecology of administration", "The politics of administration, the administrative actor, delegation", "Administrative audit and control element of Administrative Law"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 212', 'Local Government Studies', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '200 Level', 'second', 2, 'The course introduces students to the concept of Local Government and Local Administration; problems of Local Government administration; powers, functions, finances, staffing and rural development.', '["The course introduces students to the concept of Local Government and Local Administration", "Problems of Local Government administration", "Powers, functions, finances, staffing and rural development"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 244', 'Environmental Politics and Sustainable Development', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '200 Level', 'second', 2, 'The course introduces students to the basic concepts of environmental politics and sustainable development; environmental political theory; capitalization and environmental degradation; the role of global environmental movements in environmental protection and conservation; nature of the State and environmental problems in Africa; mechanism of protection and preservation, neoliberal politics and sustainable development.', '["The course introduces students to the basic concepts of environmental politics and sustainable development; environmental political theory", "Capitalization and environmental degradation", "The role of global environmental movements in environmental protection and conservation", "Nature of the State and environmental problems in Africa", "Mechanism of protection and preservation, neoliberal politics and sustainable development"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 252', 'Foundations of Political Economy', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '200 Level', 'second', 2, 'The course introduces students to the relationship between politics and economics; economics and determinants of politics; class analysis and political power relations; production and politics, material basis of political actions; perspectives of Political Economy: orthodox/bourgeois; Marxist; Liberal; world system or globalist; economy, space and environment; landscape analysis and modeling; Environment and society.', '["The course introduces students to the relationship between politics and economics; economics and determinants of politics", "Class analysis and political power relations", "Production and politics, material basis of political actions", "Perspectives of Political Economy: orthodox/bourgeois; Marxist; Liberal; world system or globalist", "Economy, space and environment"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 272', 'Political Ideas', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '200 Level', 'second', 2, 'The course introduces students to the major political ideas in their historical context; emphasis on concepts like Monarchism, Liberalism, Democracy, Socialism, Fascism, Anarchism, and major proponent of each.', '["The course introduces students to the major political ideas in their historical context", "Emphasis on concepts like Monarchism, Liberalism, Democracy, Socialism, Fascism, Anarchism, and major proponent of each"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 282', 'Industrial Training/Field Trip', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '200 Level', 'second', 2, 'The course involves study tours and attachment to selected international institutions, ministries, diplomatic missions and other agencies relevant to the study and practical aspects of politics, public and private administration; with written reports at the conclusion of the study tours and attachment. The students can go to Alliance Française, Goethe Institute or any other language-learning institute for language courses. They can also go for computer proficiency courses.', '["The course involves study tours and attachment to selected international institutions, ministries, diplomatic missions and other agencies relevant to the study and practical aspects of politics, public and private administration", "Written reports at the conclusion of the study tours and attachment", "The students can go to Alliance Française, Goethe Institute or any other language-learning institute for language courses, or for computer proficiency courses"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 311', 'Government and Administration of Urban Systems', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '300 Level', 'first', 2, 'The course introduces students to the problems involved in the planning and execution of major services in urban political systems, the political and economic indicators of urban areas; Population and Census as political agents of government and administration of urban systems.', '["The course introduces students to the problems involved in the planning and execution of major services in urban political systems, the political and economic indicators of urban areas", "Population and Census as political agents of government and administration of urban systems"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 321', 'Theories of International Politics', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '300 Level', 'first', 2, 'The course introduces students to the examination of the basic concepts and theories for the study of International Politics; the concept of the State, national interest, power, conflict and accommodation; systems theories, balance of power; alliances, coalition and alliances, Models, Game and Simulation; paradigms of international politics.', '["The course introduces students to the examination of the basic concepts and theories for the study of International Politics", "The concept of the State, national interest, power, conflict and accommodation", "Systems theories, balance of power; alliances, coalition and alliances", "Models, Game and Simulation; paradigms of international politics"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 361', 'Logic and Methods of Political Inquiry', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '300 Level', 'first', 2, 'The course introduces students to the scientific method; research methods in Political Science; the logic of political inquiry and the language of variables, problem formulation; development of a logical data framework; the relationship between the research format and research process; qualitative and quantitative measurements.', '["The course introduces students to the scientific method; research methods in Political Science", "The logic of political inquiry and the language of variables, problem formulation", "Development of a logical data framework; the relationship between the research format and research process", "Qualitative and quantitative measurements"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 363', 'Political Data Analysis', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '300 Level', 'first', 2, 'The course introduces students to the procedures of statistical summarization of political information with emphasis on frequency distribution, tables and basic inferential statistics; data analysis of political campaigns, elections, census figures, and budgets.', '["The course introduces students to the procedures of statistical summarization of political information with emphasis on frequency distribution, tables and basic inferential statistics", "Data analysis of political campaigns, elections, census figures, and budgets"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 371', 'History of Political Thought (Classical to Contemporary)', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '300 Level', 'first', 2, 'The course introduces students to the critical examination of selected classical political thinkers, such as Socrates, Plato, Aristotle, as well as medieval thinkers like St. Thomas Aquinas, modern and contemporary political thinkers, from Niccolo Machiavelli, Karl Marx, Jean-Jacques Rousseau, John Locke to the present, with special emphasis on the impact of their ideas on society; political thoughts of African leaders like Blyden, Senghor, Nkrumah, Nyerere, Fanon, Cabral, Azikiwe, Awolowo and Mandela.', '["The course introduces students to the critical examination of selected classical political thinkers, such as Socrates, Plato, Aristotle, as well as medieval thinkers like St. Thomas Aquinas", "Modern and contemporary political thinkers, from Niccolo Machiavelli, Karl Marx, Jean-Jacques Rousseau, John Locke to the present, with special emphasis on the impact of their ideas on society", "Political thoughts of African leaders like Blyden, Senghor, Nkrumah, Nyerere, Fanon, Cabral, Azikiwe, Awolowo and Mandela"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 302', 'Political Behaviour', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '300 Level', 'second', 2, 'The course introduces students to the framework for analysis, exploration, and understanding of politics; micro-political analysis, the place and role of psychological forces (personality, motivation, orientation and group dynamics) in politics; the place and role of socio-economic pressures in influencing political activities, voting behaviour, political corruption, elite-mass role; class struggle, and ethnicity; political culture, socialization, propaganda and political communication.', '["The course introduces students to the framework for analysis, exploration, and understanding of politics; micro-political analysis", "The place and role of psychological forces (personality, motivation, orientation and group dynamics) in politics", "The place and role of socio-economic pressures in influencing political activities, voting behaviour, political corruption, elite-mass role; class struggle, and ethnicity", "Political culture, socialization, propaganda and political communication"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 312', 'Comparative Federalism', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '300 Level', 'second', 2, 'The course introduces students to the theories of comparative federalism, with particular reference to such countries as the USA, USSR, Canada, Germany, India and Nigeria.', '["The course introduces students to the theories of comparative federalism", "With particular reference to such countries as the USA, USSR, Canada, Germany, India and Nigeria"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 322', 'American Foreign Policy and Human Security', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '300 Level', 'second', 2, 'The course introduces students to the trends in politics, principles and orientations of American foreign policy – democratic agenda, conflict resolution and management, concepts and theories of human security; Responsibility to Protect, disarmament, war on terror; American global strategic interests: unilateralism and multilateralism, intervention efforts; prospects for collective security; the U.S. and global peace and co-existence; effects of social structure and regime type, religion and modernization, globalization.', '["The course introduces students to the trends in politics, principles and orientations of American foreign policy – democratic agenda, conflict resolution and management", "Concepts and theories of human security; Responsibility to Protect, disarmament, war on terror", "American global strategic interests: unilateralism and multilateralism, intervention efforts", "Prospects for collective security; the U.S. and global peace and co-existence", "Effects of social structure and regime type, religion and modernization, globalization"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 324', 'Politics of International Economic Relations', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '300 Level', 'second', 2, 'The course introduces students to the economic basis of some of the actions and reactions in international politics, drawing materials from International Trade, World Bank and the IMF; commercial policy, capital movement; role of the IMF, World Bank and such monetary agencies; Multilateral enterprises and national power; theory of unequal exchange; the North/South problems; economic theory of national boundaries; Customs Unions and Currency Areas.', '["The course introduces students to the economic basis of some of the actions and reactions in international politics, drawing materials from International Trade, World Bank and the IMF", "Commercial policy, capital movement; role of the IMF, World Bank and such monetary agencies", "Multilateral enterprises and national power; theory of unequal exchange", "The North/South problems; economic theory of national boundaries; Customs Unions and Currency Areas"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 332', 'Public Administration and Administrative Law in Nigeria', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '300 Level', 'second', 2, 'The course introduces students to the ecology of Nigerian public administration; the civil service; field administration, public corporation, politics of financial administration; classification of government power, the concepts of delegated legislation, rule-making powers of administrative agencies as well as the parliamentary and judicial review of administrative actions and the legal liability of government.', '["The course introduces students to the ecology of Nigerian public administration; the civil service", "Field administration, public corporation, politics of financial administration", "Classification of government power, the concepts of delegated legislation, rule-making powers of administrative agencies", "The parliamentary and judicial review of administrative actions and the legal liability of government"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 364', 'Contemporary Political Analysis', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '300 Level', 'second', 2, 'The course introduces students to the contending paradigms in contemporary political analysis, their philosophical and ideological roots, as well as evaluation, elite approach, group theory, structural-functional analysis, and theories of political development.', '["The course introduces students to the contending paradigms in contemporary political analysis, their philosophical and ideological roots, as well as evaluation", "Elite approach, group theory, structural-functional analysis", "Theories of political development"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 372', 'Theory and Practice of Marxism', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '300 Level', 'second', 2, 'The course introduces students to dialectical and historical materialism, productive forces and the labour process, labour power, objects of labour and instruments of labour; production relations, modes of production, primitive communalism, slave, feudal, capitalist, socialist, communist, production of surplus value and accumulation of, exploitation and domination. Classes and class struggle; the peasant question, the labour aristocracy, the State. Bonapartism and relative autonomy of the State. The Bureaucracy and the practice of Marxism, Gender and Marxism; some historical cases, Russia, China, Eastern Europe, Cuba, prospects of Marxism in countries like Nigeria.', '["The course introduces students to dialectical and historical materialism, productive forces and the labour process, labour power, objects of labour and instruments of labour", "Production relations, modes of production, primitive communalism, slave, feudal, capitalist, socialist, communist", "Production of surplus value and accumulation, exploitation and domination", "Classes and class struggle; the peasant question, the labour aristocracy, the State", "Bonapartism and relative autonomy of the State. The Bureaucracy and the practice of Marxism, Gender and Marxism", "Some historical cases, Russia, China, Eastern Europe, Cuba, prospects of Marxism in countries like Nigeria"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 382', 'Industrial Training/Field Trip', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '300 Level', 'second', 2, 'The course involves study tours and attachment to selected international institutions, ministries, diplomatic missions and other agencies relevant to the study and practical aspects of politics, public and private administration; with written reports at the conclusion of the study tours and attachment. The students can go to Alliance Française, Goethe Institute or any other language-learning institute for language courses. They can also go for computer proficiency courses.', '["The course involves study tours and attachment to selected international institutions, ministries, diplomatic missions and other agencies relevant to the study and practical aspects of politics, public and private administration", "Written reports at the conclusion of the study tours and attachment", "The students can go to Alliance Française, Goethe Institute or any other language-learning institute for language courses, or for computer proficiency courses"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 411', 'Strategic and Defense Studies', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '400 Level', 'first', 2, 'The course introduces students to the concepts and theories of military intervention, strategic and defense studies; strategic doctrines of the superpowers; the defense politics of the major powers: NATO, Russia, China; foreign military intervention in Africa; collective security systems in Africa; the South African threat, France and Nigerian neighbours; defense economics; theories of defense expenditure; budgeting for defense; theory of collective or public goods; military alliances; politics of armament and disarmament; nuclear proliferation and Star Wars; insurgency and counter-insurgency.', '["The course introduces students to the concepts and theories of military intervention, strategic and defense studies; strategic doctrines of the superpowers", "The defense politics of the major powers: NATO, Russia, China; foreign military intervention in Africa", "Collective security systems in Africa; the South African threat, France and Nigerian neighbours", "Defense economics; theories of defense expenditure; budgeting for defense; theory of collective or public goods", "Military alliances; politics of armament and disarmament; nuclear proliferation and Star Wars; insurgency and counter-insurgency"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 413', 'Nigerian Local Government', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '400 Level', 'first', 2, 'The course introduces students to the evolution of local government in Nigeria; Local government as a third tier of government in Nigeria; issues of local government autonomy; powers of local government vis-à-vis other levels of government; Local government and development; problems of incorporation of chieftaincy and traditional institutions into local government.', '["The course introduces students to the evolution of local government in Nigeria; Local government as a third tier of government in Nigeria", "Issues of local government autonomy; powers of local government vis-à-vis other levels of government", "Local government and development; problems of incorporation of chieftaincy and traditional institutions into local government"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 421', 'Nigerian Foreign Policy', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '400 Level', 'first', 2, 'The course introduces students to the basic principles underlying Nigeria''s foreign policy; determinants of foreign policy (domestic and external); constitutional framework and governmental structure, official agencies that formulate policy; control and coordination of policy; mechanisms for implementation, Nigeria in major institutions, foreign policy and national defense; relations with major powers; impact of the changing international environment; perceptions and attitudes to the challenges of the post-Cold War Order; Nigeria''s neighbours; the effect of the civil war on Nigeria''s foreign policy; the changing pattern of Nigeria''s foreign policy roles; issues and problems of foreign policy making since 1976 and Nigeria''s pan-African role.', '["The course introduces students to the basic principles underlying Nigeria''s foreign policy; determinants of foreign policy (domestic and external)", "Constitutional framework and governmental structure, official agencies that formulate policy; control and coordination of policy", "Mechanisms for implementation, Nigeria in major institutions, foreign policy and national defense", "Relations with major powers; impact of the changing international environment", "Nigeria''s neighbours; the effect of the civil war on Nigeria''s foreign policy", "The changing pattern of Nigeria''s foreign policy roles; issues and problems of foreign policy making since 1976 and Nigeria''s pan-African role"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 423', 'International Politics of Mass Communication', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '400 Level', 'first', 2, 'The course introduces students to the concept of mass communication; human communication across international boundaries and its impact on global governance; the notion of the global village, mass communication and cultural imperialism; the issues of new international communication order; the new (social) media and political participation; issues of E-Governance in international politics.', '["The course introduces students to the concept of mass communication; human communication across international boundaries and its impact on global governance", "The notion of the global village, mass communication and cultural imperialism", "The issues of new international communication order", "The new (social) media and political participation; issues of E-Governance in international politics"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 441', 'Development Administration', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '400 Level', 'first', 2, 'The course introduces students to the notions and origins of development and development administration; national development planning; different types of Nigerian experiences in development administration; problems and prospects.', '["The course introduces students to the notions and origins of development and development administration", "National development planning", "Different types of Nigerian experiences in development administration; problems and prospects"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 443', 'Budgeting and Budgetary Process', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '400 Level', 'first', 2, 'The course introduces students to the general purposes of budgeting and types of budgets, Comparative budgetary systems of Nigeria, United Kingdom, United States of America, Russia, South Africa; general aspects of public expenditure, causes of increasing government expenditure, classification of public expenditure, fiscal policy, and its obstacle to effective revenue mobilization and management planning, programming, budgeting system.', '["The course introduces students to the general purposes of budgeting and types of budgets, Comparative budgetary systems of Nigeria, United Kingdom, United States of America, Russia, South Africa", "General aspects of public expenditure, causes of increasing government expenditure, classification of public expenditure", "Fiscal policy, and its obstacle to effective revenue mobilization and management planning, programming, budgeting system"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 451', 'Political Economy of Migration and Remittances', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '400 Level', 'first', 2, 'The course introduces students to the role of government in the management of modern economy; relationship between government and private enterprises, examines some political issues such as the role of the foreign capital in the domestic economy, the question of foreign aid, technology and expertise; the problem of development planning and administration of the economy as well as the issue of balanced regional planning, indigenization of the economy and self-reliance; the problem of dependency on the international economic system, the WTO, IMF, World Bank and Nigerian development.', '["The course introduces students to the role of government in the management of modern economy; relationship between government and private enterprises", "Examines some political issues such as the role of the foreign capital in the domestic economy, the question of foreign aid, technology and expertise", "The problem of development planning and administration of the economy as well as the issue of balanced regional planning, indigenization of the economy and self-reliance", "The problem of dependency on the international economic system, the WTO, IMF, World Bank and Nigerian development"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 473', 'Political Sociology', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '400 Level', 'first', 2, 'The course introduces students to political beliefs, values, structures, institutions and their social origins, development and functions; the social context of state power and power relationships.', '["The course introduces students to political beliefs, values, structures, institutions and their social origins, development and functions", "The social context of state power and power relationships"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 412', 'Politics and Law in Africa', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '400 Level', 'second', 2, 'The course introduces students to the comparative examination of the inter-relationship between law and politics in different African countries; the political significance of the judicial process during the colonial and independence periods; The judicial process, specifically how law arises and how it becomes institutionalized; the system of criminal justice which translates the abstract concerns of law into concrete institutions and policy.', '["The course introduces students to the comparative examination of the inter-relationship between law and politics in different African countries", "The political significance of the judicial process during the colonial and independence periods", "The judicial process, specifically how law arises and how it becomes institutionalized", "The system of criminal justice which translates the abstract concerns of law into concrete institutions and policy"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 414', 'Political Parties and Pressure Groups', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '400 Level', 'second', 2, 'The course introduces students to the organization and management of political parties, the character of party membership and recruitment, features of political parties; trade unions, interest groups, business groups, mass media, and government; the development of party programmes, electoral strategies, and pressure group activities; the appeals and election campaign techniques; standard parties and pressure group roles in legislative processes, local government dynamics and political bargaining.', '["The course introduces students to the organization and management of political parties, the character of party membership and recruitment, features of political parties", "Trade unions, interest groups, business groups, mass media, and government", "The development of party programmes, electoral strategies, and pressure group activities", "Standard parties and pressure group roles in legislative processes, local government dynamics and political bargaining"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 422', 'Politics of International Law', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '400 Level', 'second', 2, 'The course introduces students to the role of international politics in the development of international law; the impact of the nation-state system, the sources of international law; politics and international law of peace, war and neutrality; problems associated with recognition, law of the sea, sovereignty, territoriality and the outer space, the place, diplomacy and international law in resolving these and other problems; and functions of international law in the international political community.', '["The course introduces students to the role of international politics in the development of international law; the impact of the nation-state system, the sources of international law", "Politics and international law of peace, war and neutrality", "Problems associated with recognition, law of the sea, sovereignty, territoriality and the outer space", "The place, diplomacy and international law in resolving these and other problems; and functions of international law in the international political community"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 426', 'International Organizations and Institutions', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '400 Level', 'second', 2, 'The course introduces students to global political institutions and organizations such as the League of Nations and the United Nations; regional international organizations such as NATO, ECOWAS, EU, COMECON, Arab League, OPEC, UNESCO, WHO, FAO, and non-governmental international organizations.', '["The course introduces students to global political institutions and organizations such as the League of Nations and the United Nations", "Regional international organizations such as NATO, ECOWAS, EU, COMECON, Arab League, OPEC, UNESCO, WHO, FAO", "Non-governmental international organizations"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 432', 'Comparative Public Administration', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '400 Level', 'second', 2, 'The course introduces students to a comparative analysis of private large-scale organizations and public (state) administration organizations; of public administration in federal and unitary states, of the state bureaucracies, dominant career system and countries, liberal democracies, and the developing world.', '["The course introduces students to a comparative analysis of private large-scale organizations and public (state) administration organizations", "Public administration in federal and unitary states", "The state bureaucracies, dominant career system and countries, liberal democracies, and the developing world"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 434', 'Public Personnel and Financial Administration', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '400 Level', 'second', 2, 'The course introduces students to the human resources element in management of identification and selection processes in recruitment, problems of staff establishment, job deflationary staff deployment or placement, coordination, supervision and control; problems of motivating, moral, incentives, training, appraisals, discipline and labour relations; modern public management techniques, modern budgeting processes, planning, programming budgeting system (PPBS); planning agencies and their location in large scale organization; consolidation, control and accountability; and ethics of public financial management.', '["The course introduces students to the human resources element in management of identification and selection processes in recruitment, problems of staff establishment, job deflationary staff deployment or placement, coordination, supervision and control", "Problems of motivating, moral, incentives, training, appraisals, discipline and labour relations", "Modern public management techniques, modern budgeting processes, planning, programming budgeting system (PPBS)", "Planning agencies and their location in large scale organization; consolidation, control and accountability; and ethics of public financial management"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 452', 'State and Economy', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '400 Level', 'second', 2, '', '[]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  ('PSC 490', 'Project Report', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '400 Level', 'second', 4, 'The course introduces students to the details of research methodology with emphasis on the fundamentals of the research process and the format for project report based on a topic chosen from any of these fields: Political Economy, Comparative Politics, Local Government, Public Policy Analysis, Comparative Politics, Foreign Policy, Development Studies, Environmental Politics and Political Theory.', '["The course introduces students to the details of research methodology with emphasis on the fundamentals of the research process and the format for project report", "Based on a topic chosen from any of these fields: Political Economy, Comparative Politics, Local Government, Public Policy Analysis, Foreign Policy, Development Studies, Environmental Politics and Political Theory"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Political Science handbook'),
  -- Required ancillary / general studies / elective courses from other departments — real code/title/units from the timetable, description left blank pending a verified source.
  ('COS 101', 'Introduction to Computer Science', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '100 Level', 'first', 2, 'Concepts of hardware and software; basic subsystems of a digital computer; characteristics of a digital computer; devices/media; types/classes of computer emphasising the PC; history of computers and their generations. Problem-solving: algorithm, flowchart, pseudocode, program/data, running a program. Programming: introduction to Java/BASIC programming language syntax and programming. Booting and shutdown; types of operating system; user interface; managing information, computer malware (virus, etc); computer network; internet and web usage, e-mail, instant messaging, etc. Office applications; use of a statistical package and a database management system.', '["Concepts of hardware and software","basic subsystems of a digital computer","characteristics of a digital computer","devices/media","types/classes of computer emphasising the PC","history of computers and their generations","Problem-solving: algorithm, flowchart, pseudocode, program/data, running a program","Programming: introduction to Java/BASIC programming language syntax and programming","Booting and shutdown","types of operating system","user interface","managing information, computer malware (virus, etc)","computer network","internet and web usage, e-mail, instant messaging, etc","Office applications","use of a statistical package and a database management system"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Computer Science course outline'),
  ('GEO 131', 'Introduction to Map Work & Practical Geography', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '100 Level', 'first', 2, 'Types of maps. Scales, Grid systems and Grid references. Bearings. Conventional symbols. Map reduction and enlargement. Areas and distances. Map reading: identification and interpretation of features of relief, drainage, vegetation and human occupance. Interpretation of maps of selected areas.', '["Types of maps. Scales, Grid systems and Grid references. Bearings", "Conventional symbols. Map reduction and enlargement", "Areas and distances", "Map reading: identification and interpretation of features of relief, drainage, vegetation and human occupance", "Interpretation of maps of selected areas"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Geography handbook'),
  ('GSP 101', 'The Use of English I', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '100 Level', 'first', 2, 'Man, Society and Language - The Nature, Characteristics and Functions of Language, Human Communication & Language, The English Language and the Nigerian society, World English, Levels and Varieties of English — formal, informal, standard, etc., English in Literature and the Media.

Vocabulary of English - Types, Method of Vocabulary Development, Synonyms, Antonyms, Homonyms, Acronyms, Paronyms, Affixation and other morphological processes, English Language Register, diatypes and dialects.

Listening skill - The listening skill discussed as a receptive and reciprocal activity, Nature, Types, Purposes and Factors that affect Listening, Strategies and Aids for Effective Listening.

Reading Skill - The concept of reading as a linguistic organization and a vehicle of communication. Reading Problems, Levels of Reading, Types of Reading, Causes and Remedies of Reading Failures, Reading Techniques & Strategies (Scanning, Skimming, Phrase reading, Intensive & Extensive reading, Exploiting the topic sentence for main ideas), Reading for details, Reading for evaluation and inference, Reading with questions - SQ3R, PR3, Methods for understanding difficult words in a reading text, Literature reading for study, analysis and comment.

Speaking & Communication Skills - Nature, Process & Development, Principles of Public Speech Making and Social Interaction, The Speech Sounds of English and their Articulation, Phonetic Transcription and Practical Speech Work.

Study Techniques - Choosing study centers and discussion groups, Note-taking during lectures, and from audio-visual equipment, Note-making techniques during private reading and literature search, Summary & Transcoding Techniques, Retrieving information from notes, The dictionary as a study guide.

Basic Research Methods & Term Paper Writing - Research – meaning & nature, Types & Methodology; Data in the Research Process, The Research Report, Process and Techniques, Documentation in Research Reports: Process, Types and Methods, Abbreviations in Research Reports, The term paper as a miniature research report, Practical term paper writing.

Course Evaluation & Grading - Students must attend at least 75% of the lectures to qualify for examination in the course.', '["Man, Society and Language - The Nature, Characteristics and Functions of Language, Human Communication & Language, World English, Levels and Varieties of English", "Vocabulary of English - Types, Method of Vocabulary Development, Synonyms, Antonyms, Homonyms, Acronyms, Paronyms, Affixation and other morphological processes", "Listening skill - Nature, Types, Purposes and Factors that affect Listening, Strategies and Aids for Effective Listening", "Reading Skill - Reading Problems, Levels and Types of Reading, Causes and Remedies of Reading Failures, Reading Techniques & Strategies, Reading for evaluation and inference", "Speaking & Communication Skills - Principles of Public Speech Making and Social Interaction, Phonetic Transcription and Practical Speech Work", "Study Techniques - Note-taking, Note-making, Summary & Transcoding Techniques", "Basic Research Methods & Term Paper Writing - The Research Report, Documentation, Abbreviations, practical term paper writing"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Mechanical Engineering handbook'),
  ('GSP 105', 'Introduction to Natural Science I', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '100 Level', 'first', 2, '', '[]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Social Sciences course handbook'),
  ('GSP 111', 'Use of Library and Study Skills', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '100 Level', 'first', 2, 'Overview of Library: concepts, history, types and functions. Uses in academic libraries; organization of university library and library users. Library processes and procedures. Acquisition process, Cataloging and classification, LC Scheme, in-House Scheme, DDC. Serials process and circulation processes. Access tools in Library resources: Library catalogues, Indexes, Abstracts, Current contents information in the library. Reference sources: types of reference sources and services. Web resources and online resources. Overview of Databases, Online search strategies for information retrieval. Referencing and citation styles for information reporting. Concept of plagiarism. Learning skills and research skills, ICT skillsets: types of learning and information policies.', '["Overview of Library: concepts, history, types and functions. Uses in academic libraries; organization of university library and library users", "Library processes and procedures. Acquisition process, Cataloging and classification, LC Scheme, in-House Scheme, DDC. Serials process and circulation processes", "Access tools in Library resources: Library catalogues, Indexes, Abstracts, Current contents information", "Reference sources: types of reference sources and services. Web resources and online resources", "Overview of Databases, Online search strategies for information retrieval. Referencing and citation styles for information reporting. Concept of plagiarism", "Learning skills and research skills, ICT skillsets: types of learning and information policies"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Mechanical Engineering handbook'),
  ('GSP 102', 'The Use of English II', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '100 Level', 'second', 2, 'Part A: Basic Grammar: Introduction. The concept of grammar and its place in language teaching and learning. Parts of speech and their functions (treated in detail). Closed and open class items in parts of speech, Nominalization, Grammatical Structures: the phrase, the clause and the sentence. Elementary Clause Analysis, Sentence Types, Elements and Patterns. Agreement (Grammatical agreement, Notional agreement, Proximity agreement) Agreement with the correlatives. Direct and Reported Speech, Error typology identification and correction.

Part B: Varieties of writing. Introduction (The Meaning, Nature and Purpose of Writing, Writing Types or Genres and their Characteristics). The paragraph as the basic unit of an essay (Types, Development of the Paragraph, Methods of Paragraph Development, The thesis statement). Point of view and style in writing. Qualities of a good piece of writing: Form, Diction and Content in writing. The Mechanics of Writing: punctuation, spelling and capitalization.

Part C: Writing Genres - Planning and choosing your theme. Deciding your genre. Choosing and developing your plot. Point of view, setting and characterization. Using the language that works. Essay Writing — Narration, Description, Exposition and Argumentation. Technical Writing: Letter Writing, Memorandum Writing, Speech Writing, Agenda and Minutes, own story for practice, Computer-linked writing, types, style, language, and process.', '["Part A: Basic Grammar - The concept of grammar, Parts of speech, Grammatical Structures, Sentence Types, Agreement, Direct and Reported Speech, Error typology", "Part B: Varieties of writing - Meaning, Nature and Purpose of Writing, the paragraph as the basic unit of an essay, the thesis statement, Qualities of a good piece of writing, Mechanics of Writing", "Part C: Writing Genres - Planning and choosing your theme, plot, point of view, setting and characterization", "Essay Writing - Narration, Description, Exposition and Argumentation", "Technical Writing - Letter Writing, Memorandum Writing, Speech Writing, Agenda and Minutes"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Mechanical Engineering handbook'),
  ('GSP 106', 'Introduction to Natural Science II', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Political Science', '100 Level', 'second', 2, '', '[]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Social Sciences course handbook'),
